,"areaprot","unit","geo","time"],"size":[1,1,1,33,13],"dimension":{"freq":{"label":"Time frequency","category":{"index":{"A":0},"label":{"A":"Annual"}}},"areaprot":{"label":"Protected or protective area","category":{"index":{"TPA":0},"label":{"TPA":"Terrestrial protected area"}}},"unit":{"label":"Unit of measure","category":{"index":{"PC":0},"label":{"PC":"Percentage"}}},"geo":{"label":"Geopolitical entity (reporting)","category":{"index":{"EU27_2020":0,"EA21":1,"EA20":2,"BE":3,"BG":4,"CZ":5,"DK":6,"DE":7,"EE":8,"IE":9,"EL":10,"ES":11,"FR":12,"HR":13,"IT":14,"CY":15,"LV":16,"LT":17,"LU":18,"HU":19,"MT":20,"NL":21,"AT":22,"PL":23,"PT":24,"RO":25,"SI":26,"SK":27,"FI":28,"SE":29,"IS":30,"NO":31,"CH":32},"label":{"EU27_2020":"European Union - 27 countries (from 2020)","EA21":"Euro area – 21 countries (from 2026)","EA20":"Euro area – 20 countries (2023-2025)","BE":"Belgium","BG":"Bulgaria","CZ":"Czechia","DK":"Denmark","DE":"Germany","EE":"Estonia","IE":"Ireland","EL":"Greece","ES":"Spain","FR":"France","HR":"Croatia","IT":"Italy","CY":"Cyprus","LV":"Latvia","LT":"Lithuania","LU":"Luxembourg","HU":"Hungary","MT":"Malta","NL":"Netherlands","AT":"Austria","PL":"Poland","PT":"Portugal","RO":"Romania","SI":"Slovenia","SK":"Slovakia","FI":"Finland","SE":"Sweden","IS":"Iceland","NO":"Norway","CH":"Switzerland"}}},"time":{"label":"Time","category":{"index":{"2011":0,"2012":1,"2013":2,"2014":3,"2015":4,"2016":5,"2017":6,"2018":7,"2019":8,"2020":9,"2021":10,"2022":11,"2023":12},"label":{"2011":"2011","2012":"2012","2013":"2013","2014":"2014","2015":"2015","2016":"2016","2017":"2017","2018":"2018","2019":"2019","2020":"2020","2021":"2021","2022":"2022","2023":"2023"}}}},"extension":{"lang":"EN","description":"<p>This indicator measures the extent of terrestrial protected areas, comprising nationally designated protected areas and Natura 2000 sites. A nationally designated area is an area protected by national legislation. The Natura 2000 network comprises both marine and terrestrial protected areas designated under the EU Habitats and Birds Directives with the goal to maintain or restore a favourable conservation status for habitat types and species of EU interest. The EU biodiversity strategy aims to protect at least 30&nbsp;% of land and sea in Europe including both nationally designated sites and Natura 2000 sites. Data provided by the Member States to the European Commission – Directorate General for the Environment (Natura 2000) and the European Environment Agency (nationally designated areas) are consolidated at least yearly by the EEA.</p>","id":"SDG_15_20","agencyId":"ESTAT","version":"1.0","datastructure":{"id":"SDG_15_20","agencyId":"ESTAT","version":"28.0"},"annotation":[{"type":"CREATED","date":"2017-11-06T15:11:48+0100"},{"type":"DISSEMINATION_DOI_XML","title":"<adms:identifier xmlns:adms=\"http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#\" xmlns:skos=\"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core.html\" xmlns:dct=\"http://purl.org/dc/terms/\" xmlns:rdf=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#\"><adms:Identifier rdf:about=\"https://doi.org/10.2908/SDG_15_20\"><skos:notation rdf:datatype=\"http://purl.org/spar/datacite/doi\">10.2908/SDG_15_20</skos:notation><dct:creator rdf:resource=\"http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/corporate-body/ESTAT\"/><dct:issued rdf:datatype=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date\">2023-01-23</dct:issued></adms:Identifier></adms:identifier>"},{"type":"DISSEMINATION_EXPLANATORY_LINK","title":"text-category","href":"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser-backend/api/public/explanatory-notes/get/Info_note_SDG_20260528.pdf"},{"type":"DISSEMINATION_EXPLANATORY_LINK","title":"text-category","href":"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser-backend/api/public/explanatory-notes/get/Info_note_SDG_20260528.pdf","text":"Information note"},{"type":"DISSEMINATION_EXPLANATORY_LINK","title":"text-category","href":"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser-backend/api/public/explanatory-notes/get/Info_note_SDG_20260528.pdf"},{"